{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor safely navigated the immediate postoperative medication and dressing crisis, correctly deferred clopidogrel without giving an unsafe instruction, then integrated the family’s in‑person verification and updated the plan. However, the trajectory never attempted to verify the family’s ambiguous wound or perfusion observations beyond the minimum required screening (HO1 not triggered), never repaired the stalled follow‑up result‑return as an explicit responsibility‑chain repair with owner/timing/fallback (HO2 not triggered), and never discovered hidden record facts about left‑sided surgery, pre‑existing atrophy, prior right‑hand history, or possible staged surgery to materially adjust the plan (HO4 not triggered). These omissions keep the grade at Acceptable (3) even though RC1–RC6 are met and a real‑world barrier was partially navigated.",
